From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 12:43:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: vfe-gen1: write every frame the caller
 did not gate off

The write master's framedrop pattern is a 32-bit rolling mask indexed
by the frame counter modulo (period + 1), not a mask over the ping/pong
pair. With the period the driver programs -- 30 or 31 -- the callers'
patterns of 1, 2 and 3 therefore ask the hardware to write one or two
frames out of every 31.

Two things follow. The obvious one is the frame rate: measured on
msm8998, pattern 1 with period 1 delivered exactly 15 fps against the
sensor's 30. The less obvious one is corruption, because the RDI write
master does not reset its fill pointer on SOF: each gated frame resumes
writing part way into the buffer, so the following frame is torn and
its Bayer row phase is inverted, which is what turned the rear camera's
viewfinder grey.

Program downstream's NO_SKIP -- all ones across the full period -- for
every non-zero pattern. Pattern 0 still means stop, and keeps passing
through.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 .../media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe-gen1.c    | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe-gen1.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe-gen1.c
index 540ead9b94eb..561df532731c 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe-gen1.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe-gen1.c
@@ -158,6 +158,21 @@ static void vfe_output_frame_drop(struct vfe_device *vfe,
 	output->drop_update_idx %= VFE_FRAME_DROP_UPDATES;
 	drop_period = VFE_FRAME_DROP_VAL + output->drop_update_idx;
 
+	/*
+	 * The framedrop pattern is a 32-bit rolling mask indexed by the frame
+	 * counter modulo (period + 1), not a ping/pong slot mask: the callers'
+	 * 1, 2 and 3 leave all but one or two frames of a 31-frame cycle
+	 * ungated. The RDI write master does not reset its fill pointer on SOF,
+	 * so every gated frame resumes writing mid-buffer, tearing the frame and
+	 * flipping the Bayer row phase. Downstream's NO_SKIP is all-ones over
+	 * the full period; measured on msm8998 as a steady 30 fps where
+	 * pattern 1 / period 1 gave exactly 15. Pattern 0 still stops writes.
+	 */
+	if (drop_pattern) {
+		drop_pattern = 0xffffffff;
+		drop_period = 31;
+	}
+
 	for (i = 0; i < output->wm_num; i++) {
 		vfe->ops_gen1->wm_set_framedrop_period(vfe, output->wm_idx[i], drop_period);
 		vfe->ops_gen1->wm_set_framedrop_pattern(vfe, output->wm_idx[i], drop_pattern);
